{
  "id": "flow_coefficient_cv_vs__flow_factor_kv",
  "title": "Flow Coefficient Cv vs. Flow Factor Kv",
  "description": "Comparing flow coefficients Cv to flow factors Kv. Convert between imperial (Cv) and metric (Kv) flow coefficients for control valves.",
  "type": "calculator-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Flow Coefficient Cv vs. Flow Factor Kv\n\nThe flow coefficient - **Cv** - or the flow factor - **Kv** - are commonly used to specify capacities of control valves.\n\n## Flow Coefficient - Cv\n\nBased on the imperial units system, the flow coefficient **Cv** is defined as:\n- The flow of water through a valve at 60°F in U.S. gallon/minute at a pressure drop of 1 lb/in²\n- Commonly used in the U.S.\n\n## Flow Factor - Kv\n\nThe metric equivalent based on the SI-system, the flow factor **Kv** is defined as:\n- The flow of water with temperature ranging 5-30°C through a valve in cubic meters per hour (m³/h) at a pressure drop of 1 bar\n- Commonly used outside the U.S.\n\n## Conversion Formulas\n\n- **Cv = 1.16 × Kv**\n- **Kv = 0.862 × Cv**"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "cv_value",
          "label": "Flow Coefficient (Cv)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 10,
          "unit": "gal/min/psi"
        },
        {
          "id": "kv_value",
          "label": "Flow Factor (Kv)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 8.62,
          "unit": "m³/h/bar"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "kv_from_cv",
          "label": "Kv (calculated from Cv)",
          "formula": "inputs.cv_value * 0.862",
          "unit": "m³/h/bar",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "cv_from_kv",
          "label": "Cv (calculated from Kv)",
          "formula": "inputs.kv_value * 1.16",
          "unit": "gal/min/psi",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
